WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.310
That’s it!

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.940
You’re amazing, Kai.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:04.650
Is that so?

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.610
Yeah.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.070
That’s it.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.030
Try bending it a bit more.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:09.980
Here?

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.200
Yeah.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.910
Will you guys cut it out already?

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:13.320
Huh?

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.580
I mean, why are you, an
American representative, over here?!

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.200
My match is already over,

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.420
so I can be wherever I want, right?

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.330
Exactly.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:23.670
You moron!

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.540
My match isn’t over yet.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.630
I can’t possibly practice next to the enemy.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:34.330
It’s all right. I have no interest in a
baldy, a baldy’s bread or a baldy’s match.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:35.830
Exactly.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.340
It’s not good to be short-tempered, Baldy.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.960
Don’t you just hate a person
whose hair and temper are both short?

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:41.090
Exactly.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.470
What’s with them?

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:46.300
Suddenly going out together... you stupid couple!

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.060
With this, I can’t concentrate on practicing for the finals.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:56.230
Where are you going?

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.820
Is your work proceeding smoothly?

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:58.440
Kuro-yan?

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.780
You see...

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.320
The kitchen’s been kinda taken over by two idiots–

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:04.450
Don’t make excuses!

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.830
With Suwabara having lost, if
you’re to lose now, Japan will lose.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.950
Our fate depends on you.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:19.380
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.340
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.590
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.920
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:32.180
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:36.100
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.380
Revolutionizing the bread industry!

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:19.970
If I’m to lose, then the Japanese team loses.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.180
I know that already.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:26.020
But, my opponent is <i>that</i> Shachihoko.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.470
He’s not an opponent who I can win against easily in my present state.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.850
But, having said that, I can’t think of a single way to win.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.940
And I don’t have confidence that I can win either.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:39.490
Why must I carry the burden of everything
when we’re hanging precariously off the cliff?

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.990
What in the world am I supposed to do?

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.740
You great big idiot!

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.620
Wh-Wh-Why is the manager here?!

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.370
It’s not just the manager, Kawachi-san.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.460
Tsukino!

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.710
Kanmuri!

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.340
And... Who were you again?

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.420
You ungrateful wretch.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.590
But, what are you guys doing here?!

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.930
With all of you here, isn’t the store empty?

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.600
The store doesn’t matter one tiny bit.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.470
That’s not true, but...

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:14.440
I didn’t think that you’d fallen this low, Kawachi.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.570
You’re close to the all-important
match and far from getting ready for it.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.650
All you’re doing is complaining
and feeling sorry for yourself.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.490
Th... That’s...

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:28.410
I invited your family to the finals, but
something like this would just sadden them.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.120
Th... That’s true...

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.830
Wait. What do you mean?!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.210
You invited my family to the finals?!

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:36.960
Exactomundo.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.710
Why did you do something like...

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.630
Listen.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:46.050
To my family, I’m the hero who
made it to the Pantasia Main Branch.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:52.390
In front of the family who
thinks that, if I were to lose...

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:55.520
that would make them just as sad, wouldn’t it?

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:00.070
You dumbass.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.820
I don’t even feel like hitting cowardly scum like you.

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:09.070
Kawachi-san.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.290
Open this and see.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:14.580
That’s what you gave me when I was leaving...

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.120
That’s right.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:28.600
Kawachi Kyou...

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:29.390
tarou?

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.510
My father?!

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:35.480
Have you heard the story of this man?

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.810
He knew that he didn’t have as much
talent at breadmaking as most people.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:42.160
Nobody passes this time.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:45.030
Yet, no matter how many times he failed...

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.820
See you again next year.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.620
No matter how much shame he had to bear...

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.870
He never gave up and never ran away.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.420
That old man is here again.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:04.420
He acted upon his beliefs and his will.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:07.220
He was a man who stood up for
his dreams time and time again.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:09.510
Kawachi Kyoutarou.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.640
That’s right.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.720
I’m talking about your father.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.470
Kawachi-san!

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:19.060
It’s true that you made it to the Pantasia Main Branch.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:19.650
But!

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.320
Afraid of losing, you’ve not
tried to face up to the pressure,

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.990
in order to preserve the image your family has of you.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.610
If Kawachi Kyoutarou were to see you now...

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.490
I wonder what he’d think...

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.660
Facing your dreams, unafraid of anything.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.080
Right now, you don’t have the will for that at all.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.880
It’s all right for you to disappoint all of us.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.920
But...

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:49.340
Please, just don’t disappoint your splendid father.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.820
What’s wrong, Kyousuke?

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.820
You’re looking down in the dumps.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:12.820
Bread should not be made when you’re suffering.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.370
While making something delicious,
you should make it like you’re having fun.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.870
You’re my son.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.870
Can’t be helped if you’re a little clumsy.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.790
But... never give up, no matter what.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.380
Never run away.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:30.970
Always follow your dreams with everything you’ve got.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.100
Dad...

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.230
I wonder if this will do it?

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.070
He tends to be strongest when he’s cornered.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:50.320
If you consider how much he’s been slacking lately, he needs to be cornered this much.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.950
Yep.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:55.370
I think it was worth all of us coming at the expense of shutting down the store suddenly.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:59.870
Though, I was almost left behind to mind the store.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.710
Now we just have to wait and
see how serious Kawachi-san gets.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.000
I’m home.

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:10.710
Wh-What’s this?!

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:13.380
The word “impossible” does not exist in my dictionary.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:15.010
“Impossible” does not exist.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.850
Ka-Kawachi?

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:21.070
Listen up.
And listen well, <i>Japan</i>-freakboy.

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:26.110
As of today, I’m going to
revolutionize the bread industry.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:26.560
Idiot.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.820
Y-You’re going to revive Kakuei?!

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:29.440
Tanaka Kakuei was a former
Prime Minister of Japan
Y-You’re going to revive Kakuei?!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:32.080
Tanaka Kakuei was a former
Prime Minister of Japan

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:33.490
That’s impossible!

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:37.620
Even I know that former Prime
Minister Tanaka died a long time ago.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.370
That’s not it, you idiot!

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.120
I’m going to lead a revolution.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:43.710
What was that?!

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.580
Your wife is Kakuei?!

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:46.750
A new truth unfolds...

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.170
Well, you see...

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.630
I don’t know.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:51.760
You idiot!

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:52.970
Just leave.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:55.300
Ouch!

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:59.310
Hey, be quiet will you?

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:00.310
Manager?!

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.810
So, what in the world did you all come here to do?

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.480
We’ve come to eat monaka in Monaco.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.810
And, leaving that aside...

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:12.030
Was there anything different about Kawachi-san?

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.490
Come to think of it...

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.570
He was saying something about Kakuei.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:17.070
Kakuei?

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:18.280
It’s probably “kakumei.”

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.290
A revolution, huh?

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:23.790
Looks like we can really
look forward to this.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:32.090
If I think about it, after I got info Pantasia’s Main Branch, I didn’t really have an aim.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:33.840
I’ve been half-assed about things.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.510
I’ve been depending on Azuma and
Suwabara entirely during this tournament.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.810
And that’s probably because I’ve
not been serious about anything lately.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.480
The Pantasia Main Branch.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:49.940
That was my objective in order to support my family.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:54.940
But... if I just wanted to make money,
then I didn’t really need to be a baker.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:55.530
Kawachi Kyoutarou

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:58.660
The reason that I really wanted to become a baker...
Kawachi Kyoutarou

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.160
It’s because I wanted to become cool like you, Dad.
Kawachi Kyoutarou

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:04.240
It’s because I wanted to become cool like you, Dad.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:09.630
You caused your family a lot of
problems for the sake of your dream.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.840
And in the end, you died.

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:14.510
But...

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.930
I always admired you for that.

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:20.270
Listen up, Kyousuke.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:25.270
Your father believes that dinner bread is
the most widely eaten bread in the world.

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:29.270
Right now, I’m still a pathetic baker
who’s not capable of getting into Pantasia.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:32.650
But... someday, when I get into Pantasia...

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:39.320
I want to revolutionize the bread industry by
creating the dinner bread amongst dinner breads.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:42.410
A revolution with a dinner
bread amongst dinner breads...

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:45.830
That dream is really cool.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.750
So, this is the latest sample.

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:49.830
Eat it and see?

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:53.040
Yuck.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:55.250
What is this?!

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:56.760
It really stinks!

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.340
Since it’s something you eat every day...

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:01.130
I tried mixing in herbs that are good for your health.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:02.970
Hey, old man...

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.140
I guess I’ll bear poverty a little longer.

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:06.680
Thank you.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.180
Hey, who you calling an old man?!

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:12.690
Sometimes it hurt, though, that the
only thing cool about you was your dreams.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:16.900
Dad, since you died so early...

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.400
I couldn’t really learn much from you.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:21.530
But...

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:24.160
the picture of you always believing in your dreams...

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.620
and working hard always...

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.910
is still burnt within my eyes.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:30.960
Listen up.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.920
It seems that I have a little
more talent for bread than you did.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:38.420
So... I will fulfill that dream of yours at this tournament.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.300
A dinner bread to revolutionize the bread industry.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.930
With “Victory”!

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:53.540
The day before the 2nd match of the finals

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.440
All right! It’s done.
The day before the 2nd match of the finals

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:57.980
The day before the 2nd match of the finals

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:00.690
Let’s start with the ears.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:06.450
This is...!

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.870
This light taste and comforting fragrance...

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.870
I feel like I’m flying in the sky!

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:16.170
These ears are amazing.

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:22.930
Before I could stop myself,
I had a reaction to my own bread.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:25.390
But... why had my nose elongated as well?

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.140
The problem is the dough inside.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.780
This is pretty bad, even for me.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:45.240
This time I had a reaction because of how bad it was.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.500
At this rate, the ears are completely wasted.

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:52.000
He seems to be keeping busy with all his reactions.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.910
What could this possibly mean?

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:57.210
How could the insides be awful when the ears are good...

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.250
He’s mixing in something other than flour.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:04.010
This fragrance probably is...

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.050
It’s dattan soba.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.260
Dattan soba?

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:12.730
Dattan soba is something that has been eaten
by the Yi tribe in China from times immemorial.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:17.350
It contains over 100 times more of
the antioxidant rutin than normal soba.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:21.980
The theme this time is to make a
dinner bread that you’d eat every day.

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:25.400
Kawachi-san is probably frying to make something
that’s delicious and good for your health.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:26.780
And he failed.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.030
Oui.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:30.170
In order to mix soba flour into bread,

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:33.620
you have to pay attention to the baking time or it tastes bad.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:36.290
This is probably the first time Kawachi-san is trying this.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.460
So, it’s not surprising for it to not go well.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:42.300
But, the match is tomorrow.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:44.670
It might be a good idea to advise him a little...?

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:46.300
Manager?

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:48.300
I can’t advise him!

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.050
Why not?

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:52.310
He’s come this far by himself.

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:55.810
I want him to complete it on his own as well.

00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:58.070
B-But...

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.280
Another failure.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:14.620
This is no better than Dad’s herb bread.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:16.500
Dad...

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.000
I wonder if this is as far as I can get...

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:21.710
I wonder...

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:24.210
Manager! What are you doing?!

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:27.970
Weren’t you disappointed in scum like me?

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:29.550
I was.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:33.140
But, if you’re to lose, it would cause problems for us as well.

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:34.970
So, we can’t just afford to let you be.

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:36.480
Especially not if...

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.020
you’ve had a change of heart

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:42.980
and turned into someone who’s trying
to make something truly spectacular.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:49.200
Then, you’re going to tell me what I must
do in order to make this bread delicious?

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.820
No, I won’t!

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.580
Then, what did you come here to do?

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.210
You’re scum, and a baldy!

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.630
I’m shortening it to scaldy!

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:05.250
You always do that and try to depend on others!

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:07.920
That’s why you never mature!

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:12.140
Once, I tried making a bread good
for your body by mixing in tea leaves,

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.930
and I failed miserably.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.600
But, I figured out how to fix the problem on my own.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:24.270
Well, a scaldy like you probably wouldn’t
understand the heart of that kind of artisan.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:26.360
Scaldy. Scaldy. Scaldy. Scaldy.

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:29.950
I was planning on figuring it out on my own!

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:31.910
You came here on your own volition!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:32.410
Scaldy. Scaldy. Scaldy.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.200
If you’re not going to help, then get out.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.370
What’s with him?!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.410
Did he just come here to boast?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.000
Come to think of it...

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.300
That old man said something
about putting tea leaves into bread and

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.970
figuring out how to solve the problem on his own...

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.430
What did he mean?

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:55.350
I mean, tea leaves are pretty nasty when eaten.

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:57.430
Usually, you just use them to make tea.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.220
Tea, huh?

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:03.940
That old man put tea into the dough instead of tea leaves.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.520
But...

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.520
I’m using soba.

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:09.490
Unlike tea, even on adding water, it won’t...

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:10.570
I see!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.160
I got it!

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:14.200
Nice assist, Manager.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.240
But, didn’t you say something about not advising him?

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:19.200
I wonder what you’re talking about...

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.920
All I did was boast about the past.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:31.470
Watch me, Dad.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:34.680
I have friends who help me out in times of need.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:38.180
I’m really blessed when compared
to you, since you were always alone.

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:43.390
Looks like I owe them another one.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:45.310
But...

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:47.980
I’ll be sure to pay off this debt.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:53.070
I’ll win with my Victory bread.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:58.990
The day of the 2nd match of the finals

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:02.830
And we’re starting the second match of the finals.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:07.330
The examiner will be me, Pierrot,
now a one-time-offense criminal!

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.460
As usual, we don’t have much of an audience.

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.840
But, let’s not let that keep us from having fun.

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.720
I don’t care about there not being much of an audience.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:18.850
Because, this time...

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.810
my family is here to cheer me on!

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:25.310
Uh... Kyousuke!

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.900
Good luck.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:28.150
Come on, you guys, too.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:30.980
Hang in there, Bro!

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:35.400
Why can’t you be more
energetic like you were yesterday?

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:36.910
But, you’re the same, Mom.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.530
Can’t be helped.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:41.870
We were all pumped up because we heard that it was a world tournament.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.870
But this... kinda takes the wind out of your sails.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:51.670
Thanks to my family’s big cheer for me, this
hall’s just like a full Koushien Stadium to me.

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.710
There’s no way I could lose now.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:57.220
You think you can win with something like that?

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:59.970
You never change, do you?

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:03.560
In that case, then, there’s a lot more people behind me.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:08.650
Family ties are strong amongst us Italians.

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:12.400
Since I’m in the finals, my entire family came to watch!

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.110
Quality over quantity!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:21.910
Listen, you’re going to be
embarrassed in front of all your family.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.160
But, thank goodness.

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:30.580
Kawachi-san seems to be completely freed from the pressure.

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:33.210
He’s like a different person from before.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.550
That’s to be expected.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.550
In the first place,
the pressure was something

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:40.050
he created on his own from the fear that he’d lose.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:44.310
But, right now, Kawachi has the
confidence that chases away his fears

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.060
to go along with his excellent capabilities.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:51.270
His mental state right now is
completely different from before.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:56.860
Oh! Kawachi suddenly threw his flour onto the floor.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:58.450
What secret plan is this?

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.450
Umm... I got a little too
excited and it slipped from my hand.

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:04.080
Sorry.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.040
This won’t do.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.080
I must pull myself together and get going.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:22.590
Oh?! Kawachi is using some yellow fluid instead of water.

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:24.220
It’s sobayu.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.930
Sobayu?!

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:30.390
And it’s not just any sobayu!

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:32.400
It’s filled with rutin...

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:34.900
It’s dattan sobayu!

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.650
I see.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:40.530
This is the trick you’ve applied so
that it’s healthy for those who eat it.

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:44.950
He seems to be a different baldy from the semifinals.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.400
At this rate, it won’t be hard to defeat Shachihoko,

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.870
who placed third in the American team.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.370
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:52.920
You’re mistaken about something.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.000
Shachihoko was so busy training me, a newbie,

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:01.380
that he didn’t have to time to get ready for the semifinals.

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:02.430
What?

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:05.890
Then, Shachihoko placing third in the semifinals was...

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:08.560
He just wasn’t going with everything he had.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:12.440
Oh, this is amazing!

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:14.270
Wh-What’s that?!

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:17.520
It looks like a cannon!

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:23.490
This is dough that has been
wrapped around a bamboo pole.

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:26.120
This is a traditional Egyptian recipe, right?

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:30.950
I guess your criminal record isn’t for nothing, Pierrot.

00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:32.120
But, you’re right.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:35.790
The slow-food movement that’s
popular right now began in Italy.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:39.630
You could call this the ultimate slow food.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:42.300
What’s slow food?

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:44.220
To put it simply,

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:47.640
it’s a movement that began to ensure that

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:52.060
delicious traditional foods are not
wiped out by fast food and junk food.

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:53.140
Oh?

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.900
By the way,

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:58.110
since that bread is in the Egyptian style, you’ll be baking it over an open fire, right?

00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:59.150
Yep, that’s right.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:00.730
But, it’s not just any old open fire.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:03.820
I’ll be using binchoukan, the best charcoal in the world.

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:06.570
And then, I’ll be sprinkling it with this.

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:12.080
Spencer... you’ve found a terrible ingredient...

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:13.040
Yep, I have.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:17.460
After losing to Azuma in the newcomers’ battle,

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:20.150
I realized that if I only
concentrated on Nagoya,

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:24.090
I wouldn’t be able to win against world-level bakers.

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:27.260
At that time, I learned that
movement called slow food

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:31.220
had begun to get popular in my home country, Italy.

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:32.100
This is it!

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.450
And then,

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:37.600
I searched among all the slow foods of the
world and came upon a wonderful ingredient.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:42.990
Kawachi, it’s you who’s going to be
embarrassed in front of your family.

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:48.700
This ultimate slow-food cannon,
Alexandria, will be bellowing!

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.660
As expected of Shachihoko.

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:56.210
It’s certain that he’s not an
opponent I’d win against easily.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:57.580
But!

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.840
My strategy is not limited to dattan soba!

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:03.840
C-Croissant dough?!

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:08.220
And, this doesn’t look like regular croissant dough!

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:10.400
That croissant dough seems like

00:22:10.400 --> 00:22:14.350
it’s been made in a completely different manner from my <i>Lupan</i>.

00:22:15.940 --> 00:22:19.730
You seem to be up to something incredible.

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:20.610
Right, Baldy?

00:22:22.190 --> 00:22:24.650
Watch me, Dad.

00:22:29.370 --> 00:22:32.120
I’ll be starting a revolution!

00:24:05.700 --> 00:24:08.940
I'll show that clown more than a thing or two with my plain bread!

00:24:08.940 --> 00:24:11.980
Hey, what's with that outfit?
Are you trying to get this show sued?!

00:24:12.900 --> 00:24:15.040
Ladies and gentlemen of the audience, I thank you.

00:24:15.040 --> 00:24:16.460
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.460 --> 00:24:19.040
The Great Detective Pierrot!!
A Reaction you Lay your Life On!

00:24:19.040 --> 00:24:19.860
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.450 --> 00:24:22.610
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.990 --> 00:24:27.080
Dattan soba has more than 100 times the rutin of regular soba.

00:24:27.080 --> 00:24:29.910
Rutin is also known as Vitamin P
and is a variety of porphyrin.

00:24:29.910 --> 00:24:31.630
It helps your blood flow more easily.

00:24:32.080 --> 00:24:34.080
Oh?!
